# Switching off both move markers must not blank every other overlay.
#
# All text in the program shares one glyph pass: move numbers, variation labels,
# SGF markup, the coordinate margin, the evaluation's A/B/C and its board
# readout. GobanView::Render() ran that pass only when one of the two
# move-marker toggles was on — true when it was written, since back then the
# markers *were* the overlay. Everything added since joined the same buffers
# without revisiting the gate, so Last Move off + Next Move off took the
# coordinates, the markup and the whole evaluation display with them.
#
# `overlay_glyphs` is the assertion, and it exists because of this bug: every
# other key describing an overlay — `coordinates_shown`, `markup_count`,
# `eval_labels` — reported it perfectly while nothing at all was drawn. It
# counts what the glyph pass put on screen, the way `sounds_played` counts what
# was heard rather than what was asked for.
#
# The waits are `wait <ms>` rather than `wait_idle`, which is the one place in
# the suite where that is right: what is being waited for is a *frame*, and
# idleness is about engines and navigation. Every toggle below requests a
# repaint, so the wait only has to outlast one.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white human
wait_idle
# The glyph pass does not run while the intro animation is still going, and it
# is the only thing that writes the count.
wait_until camera_animating false

# Nothing is labelled on an empty board with no cursor ahead of it, so the
# count starts at nothing. Asserting this first is what makes the numbers below
# mean something.
wait 250
expect overlay_glyphs 0

# Coordinates are the plainest thing in that pass: no game state behind them,
# and they belong to the board rather than to any move. Nine columns and nine
# rows.
toggle_coordinates on
wait 250
expect coordinates_shown true
expect overlay_glyphs 18

# A move, so the markers have something of their own to draw.
click 4 4
click 4 4
wait_until move_count >= 1
wait 250
expect overlay_glyphs >= 19       # the coordinates plus the move number

# Both markers off. This is the reported case.
toggle_last_move_overlay
wait 250
toggle_next_move_overlay
wait 250

# The markers are gone — that much was always right, because
# updateLastMoveOverlay() and updateNavigationOverlay() simply do not place
# their labels — and the coordinates are still there, which is the fix. This
# read 0 before it.
expect coordinates_shown true
expect overlay_glyphs 18

# Switching the coordinates off as well leaves nothing to draw, which is the
# other half of the claim: the count follows the screen rather than reporting a
# constant, so the assertion above cannot pass by accident.
toggle_coordinates off
wait 250
expect coordinates_shown false
expect overlay_glyphs 0

# And back, with the markers still off.
toggle_coordinates on
wait 250
expect overlay_glyphs 18

# The markers come back independently of the rest.
toggle_last_move_overlay
wait 250
toggle_next_move_overlay
wait 250
expect overlay_glyphs >= 19
